      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are five key verbal de-escalation techniques for your training: maintain a calm and non-threatening posture, use clear and simple language to ensure understanding, offer genuine choices to empower the patient, listen more while speaking less without interrupting, and avoid arguing or using jargon. These strategies provide a structured, professional approach for managing agitated individuals in the ED. Would you like me to elaborate on any specific technique or suggest a role-playing exercise for your team?",
